WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.210
Every day, water climbs from
the roots of a tall tree all the

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.290
way to its highest leaves.

3
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:10.450
Yet a plant has no heart,
and no pump of any kind.

4
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.470
So what pulls the
water all that way up?

5
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.870
In this mission, you'll follow
water as it leaves the leaves as

6
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.740
vapour, through tiny
pores called stomata.

7
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:23.410
You'll see how water and minerals
travel up through the xylem,

8
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.730
and how the phloem carries
sugars around the plant.

9
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:31.110
And you'll test what makes a
plant lose water faster: heat,

10
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.070
wind, light or dry air.

11
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:38.410
Your mission: explain how water
reaches the top of a tree.
